{
  "dom_id": "step-10836",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "Let $O$ be a point on the plane. Let's consider all the points on the plane whose distance to $O$ is equal to $5\\,\\textrm{cm}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182550/assets/ba0fc787b4469b0322fa46fa072d58ae163e24dea284f3e5507306e9b30dfbf3.png)\n\nThe collection of all such points defines a geometrical shape which is called a **circle**. \n\n- The point $O$ is called the **center** of the circle.\n\n- The distance from $O$ to any point on the circle is called the **radius**.\n\nIn our diagram above, the radius is $r={\\color{black}5\\,\\textrm{cm}}.$",
  "worked_solution": "",
